<title>GERMANY: HOCKEY-CHAMPIONS' TROPHY RESULTS.</title>
<headline>HOCKEY-CHAMPIONS' TROPHY RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-06-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of play-off matches on the</p>
<p>final day of the Champions' Trophy women's hockey tournament on</p>
<p>Sunday:</p>
<p>5/6 places:</p>
<p> Britain   3   United States   0  (halftime 1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Karen Brown 16 penalty, Lucilla Wright 65, Purdy</p>
<p>Miller 65.</p>
<p>3/4 places:</p>
<p> Netherlands   5   South Korea   2  (2-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Netherlands - Carole Thate 10 penalty, Suzan van der Wielen</p>
<p>29, 41 and 56, Fleur van de Kieft 60.</p>
<p>South Korea - Choi Mi-soon 13 and 43.</p>
<p>Final:</p>
<p>Australia beat Germany 2-1 after sudden-death extra time</p>
<p>Halftime 1-1, fulltime 1-1</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Australia - Katrina Powell 8, Alyson Annan 78</p>
<p>Germany - Britta Becker 3</p>
<p>Final classification:</p>
<p>1. Australia</p>
<p>2. Germany</p>
<p>3. Netherlands</p>
<p>4. South Korea</p>
<p>5. Britain</p>
<p>6. United States</p>
</text>
